  "_guidance": {
    "overriding_deny": "Deny rules are absolute and cannot be approved interactively, even with Sean's chat approval. .env files, lock files, .secretignore, .git/, and audit/hook dirs are hard-denied. CLAUDE.md, .gitignore, and .claude/settings*.json moved to 'ask' (2026-06-10) so Claude must get Sean's per-edit approval but is not locked out.",
    "adding_new_allow": "Run the command once via 'ask' bucket. If it becomes routine, add to allow list. Review new scripts monthly per v3 Patch 4.",
    "pattern_syntax": "See docs/ai-workflow/references/CLAUDE-PERMISSION-SYNTAX.md. Patterns are GLOB not regex.",
    "secret_prevention": "Bash denies are coarse advisory filters. Real enforcement is scripts/scan-secrets.sh on Write/Edit + pre-commit hook (CLAUDE.md Rule 44)."
  }
